{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he struck at your rear, all those who lagged behind.</b> That he struck them with a blow of the tail: he would cut the circumcisions of Israel and fling them upward and say, ״This is what you chose — take your portion.״ And this is what is written: ״And render to our neighbors sevenfold into their bosom״ — render to them what they did to us regarding circumcision, which is placed in the bosom of a man. Another interpretation: what they did to the Torah, as it is said, ״refined seven times.״ What they did to the Temple, which is placed in the bosom of the world, as it is said, ״ומחיק הארץ עד העזרה התחתונה.״ And Israel said before the Holy One, blessed be He: Master of the worlds — You say to us ״Remember,״ yet we have forgetfulness; You, before whom there is no forgetfulness — ״Remember, HaShem, etc.״ ״the day of Jerusalem; those who said, Raze it, raze it, to its foundation.״ And even though the kingdom of Aram did not destroy Jerusalem, but rather the kingdom of Babylonia did — they would say thus out of joy. And why is Amalek likened to a dog? Just as a dog is eager to lap blood, so is he eager to lap the blood of Israel. And this is: ״עמלק עם לק.\"" "<b>And did not fear Elohim.</b> Regarding weights — therefore it is juxtaposed to the portion ״לא יהיה לך בביתך וגו״ — because they did not uphold the fear [appropriate to] weights, regarding which it is written concerning them ״ויראת מאלהיך״, therefore Amalek came. And this is what is written: ״False balances are an abomination to HaShem, etc.,״ and immediately after it is written: ״Pride comes, then comes shame.״ And also here it is written: ״For an abomination to HaShem is everyone who does these.״"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The closing phrase עמלק עם לק (apparently linking לק with ללקק, 'to lap') is rendered hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:27.273538928Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}